  "conclusion": "corresponds",
  "rationale": "focus rejects a malformed input or a path lacking a positive observation, then computes the declared class at that path. It normalizes first, returns that source for the empty path, returns a whole target type only when a positive entry prefixes the path, and otherwise drops the selected common prefix and normalizes retained descendants. Thus the Pair hole in the Box example survives focusing; no unknown branch or negative field becomes whole. given.typing.normalization and the view example introduce the normal form and running declarations, while their dependencies supply Pos and classAt.",
